# Microsoft Entra ID: Employee Onboarding and Group Access Management

## Project Overview

This is a hands-on Microsoft Entra ID project focused on basic Identity and Access Management (IAM).

I used a fictional company called Stevenson Technologies to simulate the process of onboarding a new employee, creating a user account, managing security groups, and reviewing account properties.

## Project Scenario

Stevenson Technologies hired a new employee named Jordan Smith as an IT Support Technician in the Information Technology department.

My task was to create the employee account and add the employee to the appropriate department security group.

## Tools Used

- Microsoft Entra admin center
- Microsoft Entra ID Free
- Web browser
- GitHub
- Google Docs

## Tasks Completed

1. Accessed the Microsoft Entra admin center.
2. Created a user account for Jordan Smith.
3. Located and verified the employee account.
4. Created a security group named `IT-Department`.
5. Added Jordan Smith to the security group.
6. Reviewed the employee account properties.

## Skills Practiced

- Microsoft Entra ID administration
- User account creation
- Identity and Access Management (IAM)
- Security group management
- Group membership administration
- Employee onboarding
- Technical documentation

## Project Files

- `documentation/Entra-ID-Lab-Report.pdf` – Detailed lab report documenting the project.
- `screenshots/` – Screenshots showing the steps performed and results.

## What I Learned

This project helped me gain practical experience navigating Microsoft Entra ID and performing basic identity administration tasks.

I learned how to create user accounts, organize employees into security groups, verify group membership, and review account properties.

## Future Improvements

I plan to expand this project by practicing:

- Employee offboarding
- Disabling and re-enabling user accounts
- Reviewing sign-in logs
- Access reviews
- Identity administration automation

## Disclaimer

This was a personal educational lab using a fictional company and employee. Stevenson Technologies and Jordan Smith are fictional and do not represent a real business or employee.

